# Benchmark results: track summaries and reproduction manifests only.
# Bulky per-request and resource time-series stay local.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!summary.md
!summary.csv
!summary.json
!summary.jsonl
!mmlu-*.json
!mmlu-*.jsonl
!**/mmlu-*/summary-run/values.json
!**/mmlu-*/summary-run/workloads.yaml
!runs.csv
!run.json
!inference.json
!benchmark-resources.json
!nodes.json
!job.json
!cache-clear-job.json
!cache-clear.json
!*pod*.json
!**/artifacts/profile_export_aiperf.json
!**/artifacts/profile_export_console.txt
# Quality checks retain the complete questions, responses, and judgments.
!**/quality-*/**/results.json
# Embedded availability figures are part of the reports (only those referenced in summary.md).
!**/availability-*/figures/observed-timeline.png
# Grafana panels embedded in HPA summaries.
!**/hpa-*/figures/grafana-*.png
!**/benchmark-suite-*/figures/benchmark-comparison.png
!**/benchmark-suite-*/verification.json
!**/benchmark-suite-*/environment.json

# GPU console renderings duplicate the structured AIPerf export.
gpu/**/artifacts/profile_export_console.txt

# Availability: keep raw evidence and unreferenced data local.
**/availability-*/evidence/
**/availability-*/summary.json

analyze-*
compare-*
history.md

# Model candidate reports retain their measurement script.
!**/model-candidates-*/probe.py

# MPS and PD reports retain analysis, aggregate tables, validation, and figures.
# Per-request exports, payloads, resource samples, and logs stay in /reports/pd/.
!gpu/mps-check-*/summary.json
!gpu/pd/*/*.md
!gpu/pd/*/*.json
!gpu/pd/*/*.csv
!gpu/pd/*/figures/*.png
!gpu/pd/*/ttft-tpot.png
!gpu/pd/*/ttft-tpot.pdf
!gpu/pd/*/goodput/*.md
!gpu/pd/*/goodput/*.json
!gpu/pd/*/goodput/*.csv
!gpu/pd/*/goodput/*.png
